  "id": "Compound::DB01229 - Disease::DOID:1324",
  "verbalization": "Paclitaxel is implicated in the development of Lung Cancer through a chain of events involving docetaxel, a closely related compound. The evidence suggests that Paclitaxel causes neutropenic enterocolitis, radiation pneumonitis, or necrotizing enterocolitis, all of which are conditions that are caused by docetaxel. Docetaxel, in turn, is known to treat Lung Cancer, indicating a potential causal pathway where Paclitaxel may contribute to the progression of the disease through its effects on the gastrointestinal and respiratory systems. The shared ancestry of Paclitaxel and docetaxel, both belonging to the tetracyclic diterpenoid class, suggests a common pharmacological mechanism that may underlie their respective effects on tissue health and cancer treatment. This integrated evidence highlights a potential role of Paclitaxel in the pathogenesis of Lung Cancer through its interaction with docetaxel, emphasizing the importance of considering these compounds in the context of their shared biological properties and therapeutic applications.",
